# === Option A: local Supabase CLI (recommended for dev — all inside Codespaces) ===
# 1. Run:  npx supabase start     (first run pulls ~8 Docker images, few minutes)
# 2. Run:  npx supabase status    → copy the API URL / anon / service_role keys below
# 3. OTP emails land in Inbucket: http://localhost:54324 (no real emails sent)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://localhost:54321
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon key from `npx supabase status`>
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service_role key from `npx supabase status`>
# (server-only — used for username→email lookups in server actions, never the browser)

# === Option B: hosted Supabase project (for going live) ===
# From your Supabase project dashboard (Settings → API)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xyzcompany.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...

# From your Cloudflare dashboard (Turnstile → Add site). Used for the
# bot-check step in the passwordless login/signup flow.
# NOT needed for local dev: leave these commented out. The bot check is
# skipped automatically whenever the keys are unset outside production —
# uncommenting placeholder values here would BREAK local login ("bot check
# failed"), because the code would try to verify against a fake key.
# Set real values only when deploying live.
# TODO(narendra): create a Turnstile site at https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/turnstile
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAA...
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=0x4AAAAAA...
